{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"---\nname: project-cledger-redaction-state\ndescription: \"conversation-ledger secret-redaction stack — what shipped (0.6.1/0.7.0), decisions made, and what's deferred\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 48648da3-5c2c-4827-96d5-7a6ed13224df\n  modified: 2026-07-21T01:19:25.689Z\n---\n\nState of conversation-ledger's redaction work as of 2026-07-20.\n\n**Shipped:**\n- 0.6.1 — scan/sync finding reports fully mask the matched span (`<redacted>` + ~20 chars context + fingerprint, zero secret characters). Closes the sync-report channel of the capture/scan feedback loop.\n- 0.7.0 — opt-in `redact.knownSecrets` (default off). `cledger redact --pattern` remembers the exact scrubbed plaintext in `.git/conversation-ledger/known-secrets.json` (local, git-invisible, beside the allowlist); capture-time redaction then exact-matches those values out of every future draft under a `known-secret` rule id. Only `--pattern` feeds it (`--all` blanks whole content); sub-8-char values dropped. Enabled globally on this machine via `~/.config/cledger/config.json`.\n- 0.7.1 — `keyword-assignment` scan rule tightened (value charset excludes code punctuation, killing the type-annotation / template-interpolation false positives; this repo went 93 -> 64 findings); known-secrets store written `0600` with perm repair on each write; tests now redirect HOME to a throwaway dir so the developer's global config can't change test outcomes.\n\n**Decisions (so the next agent doesn't re-litigate):**\n- The roadmap's original \"make capture-tier a strict superset of scan-tier\" framing was considered and **rejected** — promoting the deliberately-noisy scan rules to run at capture would silently rewrite innocent text, breaking the near-zero-false-positive invariant. The value-based learning above is the intended narrow form.\n- Store holds plaintext by necessity (fingerprints are one-way, can't drive exact matching); acceptable because `.git/` is as local-and-unshared as the transcripts, per the transport trust boundary.\n\n**Deferred, roughly by urgency:**\n1. Encrypt known-secrets at rest (OS keychain; decrypt must be non-interactive since capture runs silently every turn). `0600` already shipped.\n2. Post-push purge, re-anchor, path-based capture exclusion, auto-renormalize, harness-artifact capture, sub-turn citation anchors.\n\n**Dogfooding note:** this repo captures its own sessions. The ledger still has ~64 benign scan findings (fixtures containing literal `password=supersecret123`-style strings, which no pattern can distinguish from real secrets), so the ledger push is held back by default while code pushes fine. Sharing this session's ledger requires resolving those with `cledger allow`.\n\nRelated: [[project-ledger-ecosystem]]\n---\nname: project-ledger-ecosystem\ndescription: \"conversation-ledger is the neutral storage primitive in a 3-repo ecosystem (turnbridge captures, intent-recall retrieves); must stay maximally general/unix-composable\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837\n  modified: 2026-07-22T18:30:59.304Z\n---\n\nconversation-ledger (this repo) is the foundation of a 3-repo ecosystem, all design-stage as of 2026-07-18:\n- `../turnbridge` — captures/transfers visible conversations between coding CLIs (adapters, cursors); first producer.\n- `../intent-recall` — later evidence retrieval about repo intent; first consumer. Wants generic evidence kinds (decisions, documents), not just conversation turns, and sub-turn citation anchors eventually.\n- `/Users/evintunador/repos/BandaruDheeraj/sticky-note` (singular) — Dheeraj's shipped Node CLI (npm `sticky-note-cli`, v3) for AI-session team handoff; referenced as a structural template: git-native storage (orphan `sticky-note/data` branch + `refs/notes/sticky-note`), hook-driven capture, MCP server, field-level merge driver.\n\nStatus 2026-07-18: v0.1 implemented (TS/Node, zero runtime deps, `cledger`/`conversation-ledger` bins, npm-linked globally), 46 tests passing. Storage = one note per anchor commit under refs/notes/conversation-ledger, inline JSONL, cat_sort_uniq merges; branch-tied via commit reachability per user's explicit requirement. Global capture hooks installed in ~/.claude/settings.json and ~/.codex/config.toml (backups exist). User trusted the Codex hook via /hooks (2026-07-18, verified live: codex exec sessions auto-capture). Reasoning policy set by user: record reasoning when the provider exposes it, skip when withheld. The conversation-ledger repo itself had zero commits; captured events sit in .git/conversation-ledger/pending.jsonl until first commit.\n\nThe user's hard constraint: the ledger must stay a small standalone general utility (unix tool-composition philosophy) — storage/provenance only, no interpretation, no orchestration. Closest prior art found (2026-07): git-memento (transcripts in git notes, commit-linked); differentiators are the normalized multi-CLI schema, append-only evidence events, manifest-based redaction, content-addressed blobs under one dedicated ref. See [[feedback-liberal-small-subagents]].\n\nCorrection (2026-07-22): sync is NOT opt-in as this memory previously claimed — as shipped, the ledger ref transport is **default-on, opt-out**: first capture in a repo installs a `pre-push` hook (pushes the ledger ref alongside code, gated by secret scan) and a fetch refspec (pulls teammates' events automatically on `git fetch`/`pull`). `{\"transport\": {\"hook\": false, \"fetchRefspec\": false}}` opts out; `cledger sync` is just the explicit/manual trigger for the same thing, usable either way. See [[project-cledger-reasoning-preservation]] for where this mattered in a design decision.\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","is_error":false,"tool_use_id":"toolu_015nk7cYT5AMi6eN1REH4SoD","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"98cbc80622cab3604a994b8dfe2c60fbf8296d25","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:cef69ec2-8b5a-4e91-8078-ac955e039295","seq":32},"id":"ev1-92fe39f21e20d26367436260dcfe385e3bbfbb3b3c80da0615f02b3ddecad0cd","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-27T06:49:03.361Z","producer":{"session_id":"cef69ec2-8b5a-4e91-8078-ac955e039295","source":"claude-code","tool":"cledger","version":"0.11.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"---\nname: project-cledger-redaction-state\ndescription: \"conversation-ledger secret-redaction stack — what shipped (0.6.1/0.7.0), decisions made, and what's deferred\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 48648da3-5c2c-4827-96d5-7a6ed13224df\n  modified: 2026-07-21T01:19:25.689Z\n---\n\nState of conversation-ledger's redaction work as of 2026-07-20.\n\n**Shipped:**\n- 0.6.1 — scan/sync finding reports fully mask the matched span (`<redacted>` + ~20 chars context + fingerprint, zero secret characters). Closes the sync-report channel of the capture/scan feedback loop.\n- 0.7.0 — opt-in `redact.knownSecrets` (default off). `cledger redact --pattern` remembers the exact scrubbed plaintext in `.git/conversation-ledger/known-secrets.json` (local, git-invisible, beside the allowlist); capture-time redaction then exact-matches those values out of every future draft under a `known-secret` rule id. Only `--pattern` feeds it (`--all` blanks whole content); sub-8-char values dropped. Enabled globally on this machine via `~/.config/cledger/config.json`.\n- 0.7.1 — `keyword-assignment` scan rule tightened (value charset excludes code punctuation, killing the type-annotation / templa